<title>CHINA: Shanghai Cereals Exchange to suspend commission.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Cereals Exchange to suspend commission.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai Cereals &amp; Oils Exchange will cancel exchange commissions on trades in the soybean contracts for a month starting from next Monday to help boost business, an exchange official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The exchange hopes the measure will boost trading in soybeans, the official said.</p>
<p>The current commission is two yuan per lot (five tonnes), he said.</p>
<p>Shanghai soybean futures ended mixed on Friday on combined volume of 7,320 lots or 36,600 tonnes, down from Thursday's 47,900 tonnes.</p>
</text>
